  "theorem": "For qubit involutions X=n.sigma and Z=m.sigma, anticommutation is n.m=0. With invertible targets X0=Z0=c sigma_x, minimizing the joint Frobenius error is equivalent to maximizing e_x.(n+m)<=sqrt(2). Equality holds for n=(e_x+u)/sqrt(2), m=(e_x-u)/sqrt(2) for every unit u perpendicular to e_x, producing a circle of global minimizers. Thus universal global nearest-joint-factor uniqueness is false even when both raw targets are invertible."
